      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/trajector/{size}/1914_2.png",
      "created_at": "2017-07-22T05:39:07.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>We thought there was some ambiguity about this in the rules:</p>\n<p>During Ravage, the Invaders attack the land and then attack the Dahan.</p>\n<p>Let’s say I use a power that defends 2.</p>\n<ol>\n<li>\n<p>Do I get to defend 2 against the attack on the land, then defend 2 against the attack on the Dahan? (I.e. does the defense reduce the power of the attack?)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>If no, must I use all the defense on one of the two attacks? Can I assign some blocking points to the land and some to the Dahan?</p>\n</li>\n</ol>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:49:45.907Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 112,
      "reads": 0,
      "readers_count": 0,
      "score": 550.0,
