      "read": false,
      "user_title": "",
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "We thought there was some ambiguity about this in the rules:\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nDuring Ravage, the Invaders attack the land and then attack the Dahan.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nLet's say I use a power that defends 2.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n1. Do I get to defend 2 against the attack on the land, then defend 2 against the attack on the Dahan? (I.e. does the defense reduce the power of the attack?)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n2. If no, must I use all the defense on one of the two attacks? Can I assign some blocking points to the land and some to the Dahan?",
